[[File:Warped Terrorbird icon.png|left]]
'''Warped Terrorbirds''' are creatures found in the [[Poison Waste Dungeon]] beneath the [[Galarpos Mountains]], requiring partial completion of [[The Path of Glouphrie]] and level 56 [[Slayer]] to kill. It is recommended to wear [[earmuffs]] or a [[Slayer helmet]] while fighting them in order to halve their max hit and reduce chip damage through [[Protect from Missiles|protection prayer]] from their ranging attacks.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1754800191910072403|date=6 February 2024|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963334|archivedate=7 April 2026|quote=[How do earmuffs reduce damage from Warped Terrorbirds? Does it completely negate their ranged attacks?] I don't think so. My colleagues' code looks more like it'd halve the max hit.}} Players must have the [[crystal chime]] in their inventory to fight them, otherwise they will be invulnerable. They do '''not''' count for bird Slayer tasks, and it is not required to be on task to kill them.

Warped terrorbirds will never grow [[tolerant]] of intruders, and will remain [[Aggressiveness|aggressive]] even after staying in their tolerance region for ten minutes.{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/1703708605227192404|date=18 September 2023|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27963989|archivedate=11 May 2026|quote=[is it intentional that in the poison waste dungeon, aggro timers don't seem to have an effect? (...)] Their dev appears to have disabled that behaviour manually.}}

